  "scope": "The literal10760-slot program takes only the original cost-row, graph-matrix and demand-list roots. Actual grid-input execution traverses the original cost row to compute dimension, width and fuel. Literal pair and nil allocations construct the context and empty exponent; the actual metadata fuel root drives the unchanged binary family. Saved frames preserve all three original roots. No context, exponent, grid budget, minimum index, shifted row, packing state or result list is supplied. The same physical run returns the original guesses state-list under original minimum selection, retains input representations/source and pays halt. Empty/all-zero rows retain explicit optional-list behavior. The original-input instruction envelope still uses the frozen recursive numerical family bound; a derived polynomial grid-range envelope and final dispatcher composition remain separate. Twelve new paid physical cases cover empty/all-zero, padded, directed/loop/reversed-demand and multirow inputs; three positive whole-grid cases are explicitly natural-reference checks. Positive paid child cases remain inherited and are not recounted as whole-program physical fixtures. Initial original representations, demand encoding, H/B and dense cursor remain premises. Old operation-counter equality is not asserted."
